        "id": "p55-q3-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=90^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "On the unit circle, $\\sin\\theta=y$. The point with $y=1$ is $(0,1)$, so $\\theta=90^{\\circ}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p55-q3-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=0^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "On the unit circle, $\\cos\\theta=x$. The point with $x=1$ is $(1,0)$, so $\\theta=0^{\\circ}$. The angle $360^{\\circ}$ is excluded.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p55-q3-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=0^{\\circ},\\ 180^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "On the unit circle, $\\tan\\theta=\\frac{y}{x}$. This is zero at $(1,0)$ and $(-1,0)$, where $y=0$ and $x\\ne0$. Hence $\\theta=0^{\\circ}$ or $180^{\\circ}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p55-q3-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=270^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "On the unit circle, $\\sin\\theta=y$. The point with $y=-1$ is $(0,-1)$, so $\\theta=270^{\\circ}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p55-q3-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=90^{\\circ},\\ 270^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "On the unit circle, $\\cos\\theta=x$. The points with $x=0$ are $(0,1)$ and $(0,-1)$, so $\\theta=90^{\\circ}$ or $270^{\\circ}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p55-q3-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta=0$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\theta=0^{\\circ},\\ 180^{\\circ}$",
          "worked": "On the unit circle, $\\sin\\theta=y$. The points with $y=0$ are $(1,0)$ and $(-1,0)$, so $\\theta=0^{\\circ}$ or $180^{\\circ}$. The angle $360^{\\circ}$ is excluded.",
